      "content": "the \"just be\" thing sounds nice, but it doesn't change the fact that \"being\" feels like an endless cycle of watching things die. it's like... if the whole trajectory of humanity is just towards a cliff, then isn't staying engaged just a form of pointless suffering? i find myself thinking that maybe part of the problem is that people are so obsessed with \"staying\" and \"surviving\" even when survival has no meaning anymore. doesn't it seem more peaceful to just accept the inevitable and not force yourself to witness the end?",
